        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 165.74,
          "end": 169.27,
          "en": "We will also not fetch it from inside the PostItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 169.27,
          "end": 172.57,
          "en": "with user fact and fetch or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 172.57,
          "end": 176.9,
          "en": "Instead I expect that I get it through props so that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 176.9,
          "end": 180.7,
          "en": "in the post-grid component where we rendered a PostItems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 180.7,
          "end": 182.96,
          "en": "and where we have a list of posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 182.96,
          "end": 185.93,
          "en": "which probably is a list of JavaScript objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 185.93,
          "end": 189.77,
          "en": "with the post data where we then just forward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.77,
          "end": 193.05,
          "en": "that data we have here already into the PostItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 193.05,
          "end": 195.58,
          "en": "through props, that's the goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 195.58,
          "end": 199.8,
          "en": "So in PostItem, we can expect a couple of props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 199.8,
          "end": 202.43,
          "en": "and I will use object de-structuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 202.43,
          "end": 207.43,
          "en": "to pull those prop properties into separate constants.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 208.32999999999998,
          "end": 209.81,
          "en": "Now it is your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 209.81,
          "end": 213.35,
          "en": "It is up to you how you expect to get data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 213.35,
          "end": 217.51,
          "en": "how you expect to pass data to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 217.51,
          "end": 219.11,
          "en": "If you wanna have one prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 219.11,
          "end": 223.66,
          "en": "which carries the entire post data or multiple props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 223.66,
          "end": 226.11,
          "en": "and I will go for one prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 226.11,
          "end": 231.11,
          "en": "a post prop on props, and I'll destructure that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 231.39,
          "end": 233.86,
          "en": "So I expect that I get a post prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 233.86,
          "end": 236.78,
          "en": "and that post prop holds a JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 236.78,
          "end": 240.03,
          "en": "with multiple properties which describe the post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 240.03,
          "end": 242.57,
          "en": "and I'm now pulling out those properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 242.57,
          "end": 246.723,
          "en": "into separate constants with object de-structuring here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 247.59,
          "end": 248.933,
          "en": "And we could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 248.933,
          "end": 252.12,
          "en": "expect a title, a image, an excerpt,",
